    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d932">

                <pb facs="0726" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg610"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13521.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Canova to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aguascalientes</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-15T09:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 15, 1914, 9 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Convention met this afternoon and decided to telegraph General Zapata and
                    Governor Maytorena to suspend all hostilities. In <pb facs="0727" n="611"
                        xml:id="pg611"/> stead of telegraphing Zapata invitation to attend
                    Convention as a delegate, out of courtesy the Convention appointed a committee
                    to invite him; they will leave tonight.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canova</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
